          "Other schemes structure things differently, but the pattern is similar: orthotic and appliance benefits typically sit inside a shared annual family limit (often bundled with prosthetics or other external medical devices), and getting approval generally requires a detailed clinical motivation, supporting diagnostic evidence, a formal itemised quotation, and referral from a treating specialist rather than a general practitioner, according to one medical aid comparison resource [medicalaid.com](https://medicalaid.com/medical-aids/best-medical-aid-schemes-that-cover-prosthetics/).",
